target/

# `Cargo.lock` is deliberately *not* here. This workspace builds binaries, not
# a library, and a binary's lock file belongs in the repository: without it
# every machine and every CI run resolves its own dependency versions, so
# nobody builds the same thing twice and an upstream patch release can break
# the build with nothing to pin it back to.

# Built from `probe.cpp` by the command in `dev/qtprobe/README.md`. A compiled
# binary in a repository is a thing nobody can read and nobody can trust.
dev/qtprobe/probe

# Generated by `dev/preview`, which runs each crate's own preview binary.
crates/animation/preview/preview.html
crates/effects/preview/preview.html

# The agent guide stays local. It is instructions for whoever or whatever is
# editing this repository, not part of the compositor, and publishing it says
# nothing to anyone reading the code.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
